Vercel Web Analytics Installation Complete

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js project following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart).

## Changes Made:

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/analytics` package (v1.4.1) via npm
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json with the new dependency

### 2. Configured Analytics Component
Modified: `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx`
- Imported `Analytics` component from `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag in the RootLayout
- Follows the official Next.js App Router integration pattern

### 3. Added ESLint Configuration
Created: `frontend/.eslintrc.json`
- Configured ESLint with Next.js defaults for code quality
- Our changes pass linting with no errors

## Implementation Details:

The integration follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- The Analytics component is placed at the end of the body tag
- It will automatically track page views and web vitals
- The component is server-side rendered and optimized for performance
- Analytics will be active once the project is deployed to Vercel

## Verification:

✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ No TypeScript errors
✅ No ESLint errors in modified files
✅ All dependencies properly installed and lock file updated

## Next Steps:

To enable Web Analytics:
1. Deploy this code to Vercel
2. Navigate to your project's Analytics tab in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable Web Analytics" to activate tracking
4. After deployment, verify by checking browser DevTools Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/view`

The analytics will automatically start collecting data after enabling in the Vercel dashboard and deploying these changes.
